                <pb facs="0441" n="429" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg429"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.51A/10–744: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Iran</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Morris</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-10-07T14:00:00-04:00">October 7, 1944—2
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>610. Should question of Millspaugh’s resignation again arise Department desires
                    that you make very clear to members of the Financial Mission that the
                    Department’s attitude as expressed in the first paragraph of telegram 386 June
                    24 remains unchanged. It would not be in the interests of the United States for
                    them to resign in a body.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
